<title>GERMANY: France, Germany outline EU reform proposals.</title>
<headline>France, Germany outline EU reform proposals.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>France and Germany outlined joint proposals for reforming the European Union on Monday calling for closer cooperation on internal and external security and a shake-up of EU institutions.</p>
<p>But a joint letter by President Jacques Chirac and Chancellor Helmut Kohl to fellow EU leaders ahead of Friday's summit in Dublin left key issues vague, with two options for the appointment of a European foreign policy representative and no clear areas for the extension of majority voting.</p>
</text>
